hailing from Minnesotan cuisine. It is made with white bread, brown gravy, mashed potatoes, and pot roast. The sandwich is popular café food in rural Western Minnesota and can even be found in the Twin Cities."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-hot-beef-commercial"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_beef_commercial"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Minnesotan cuisine","cuisine/minnesotan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Gravy","ingredient/gravy"],["Mashed potato","ingredient/mashed-potato"],["Pot roast","ingredient/pot-roast"],["White bread","ingredient/white-bread"]]},{"h":"More from Minnesotan cuisine","links":[["Minnesota sushi","dish/minnesota-sushi"],["South American (sandwich)","dish/south-american-sandwich"],["Walleye sandwich","dish/walleye-sandwich"],["Wild rice salad","dish/wild-rice-salad"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/e1/Beef_Manhattan.jpg/500px-Beef_Manhattan.jpg","w":500,"h":372,"by":"Monkeyota","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beef_Manhattan.jpg"}},"dish/mango-float":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mango-float","n":"Mango float","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 3 cuisines","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mango float or crema de mangga is a Filipino icebox cake dessert made with layers of graham cracker crust, whipped cream, condensed milk, and ripe carabao mangoes. It is chilled for a few hours before serving, though it can also be frozen to give it an ice cream-like consistency. It is a modern variant of the traditional Filipino crema de fruta cake. It is also known by other names like mango refrigerator cake, mango graham float, mango royale, and mango icebox cake, among others. Crema de mangga is another version that additionally uses custard and gulaman (agar) or gelatin, as in the original crema de fruta."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mango-float"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mango_float"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine"],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao"],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":8,"links":[["Carabao mango","ingredient/carabao-mango"],["Condensed milk","ingredient/condensed-milk"],["Cracker","ingredient/cracker"],["Graham crackers","ingredient/graham-crackers"],["Ladyfinger (biscuit)","ingredient/ladyfinger-biscuit"],["Mango","ingredient/mango"],["Savoiarde PAT","ingredient/savoiarde-pat"],["Whipped cream","ingredient/whipped-cream"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Panlasang Pinoy","ref":"site/panlasangpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"panlasangpinoy.com","note":"Vanjo Merano's large library of Filipino recipes and cooking videos.","url":"https://panlasangpinoy.com/filipino-food/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Kawaling Pinoy","ref":"site/kawalingpinoy-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kawalingpinoy.com","note":"Lalaine Manalo's blog of Filipino home cooking.","url":"https://www.kawalingpinoy.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Flavours of Iloilo","ref":"site/flavoursofiloilo-blogspot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com","note":"Blog of Ilonggo home dishes from Iloilo in the Western Visayas.","url":"https://flavoursofiloilo.blogspot.com/2013/05/how-about-some-chicken-binakol.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Filipino cuisine","links":[["Adobo (Filipino dish)","dish/adobo-filipino-dish"],["Aparon","dish/aparon"],["Banana ketchup","dish/banana-ketchup"],["Champorado","dish/champorado"],["Filipino barbecue","dish/filipino-barbecue"],["Food for the gods","dish/food-for-the-gods"],["Isaw","dish/isaw"],["Kadyos, baboy, kag langka","dish/kadyos-baboy-kag-langka"],["Kadyos, m